**resources.cpp does Win32 resource interception for icon, splash, and logo assets.**

## Interface

`resources::component` derives `component_interface`; overrides `~component()`, `post_start()`, and `void* load_import(const std::string& library, const std::string& function)`.

## Behavior

`post_start()` loads `ID_ICON` and `IMAGE_SPLASH` from the module via `LoadIconA`/`LoadImageA`; `load_import()` redirects `USER32.dll` imports `LoadIconA` and `LoadImageA` to local hooks. `load_icon_a()` returns `icon` for resource ID `2`; `load_image_a()` returns `logo` for `"logo.bmp"` or `splash` for resource ID `0x64`, otherwise delegates to Win32 APIs.

## Lifecycle

`resources::component::~component()` destroys `icon`, `logo`, and `splash`; `REGISTER_COMPONENT(resources::component)` registers the component.